# ── MARK LIII — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
# NOTE: no trailing comments on these lines. Git does NOT support end-of-line
# comments in .gitignore — it treats the whole line, spaces and "#" included, as
# the pattern. Five of the entries below used to carry explanations on the same
# line, so none of them matched anything: config/api_keys.json sat untracked but
# NOT ignored, one `git add -A` away from being published. Explanations go above
# the pattern now.

# The API key lives in .env and nowhere else (core/env_config.py).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# MCP server config — may reference tokens; the example is committed instead.
mcp_servers.json
!mcp_servers.example.json

# Playwright MCP scratch output (page snapshots, traces).
.playwright-mcp/

# Settings file. No longer holds the API key, but per-plugin config can carry
# tokens for whatever a plugin talks to.
config/api_keys.json

# The dashboard's TLS private key and certificate.
config/certs/

# A LINKED WhatsApp session — committing it hands somebody your WhatsApp
# account, not merely a key.
config/whatsapp_web/

# Google OAuth tokens and client secrets (Gmail / Calendar plugins).
**/token*.json
**/client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/long_term.json
memory/*.db

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/
